{"game": "the-anacrusis", "language": "english", "appid": 1120480, "month": "2022-07", "window": 1, "start_date": 1656633600, "end_date": 1659311999, "month_true_total": 14, "quota": 14, "returned": 14, "pulled_at": "2026-09-03 00:43:58 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "119434689", "author": {"steamid": "76561199010801723", "personaname": "Megatron", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/megatron4837/", "num_games_owned": 385, "num_reviews": 52, "playtime_forever": 697, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 277, "last_played": 1717519950, "avatar": "a92d086e346591efb6878a220a78e2f1cc9a2650"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is absolutely cool like a Sci-Fi from the '70s with Left 4 Dead overtones.\nFor early release this game is pretty polished, it has co-op 4 players and there is 3 levels so far and a standoff mode with wave after wave of enemy combatants to deal with.\n\nBottom line: I suggest this game is worth getting if you like co-op shooters.", "timestamp_created": 1658744319, "timestamp_updated": 1658744319, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.51460874080657959", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "119276568", "author": {"steamid": "76561198068406488", "personaname": "RoachDoggJr", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/nintendogametube/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 45, "playtime_forever": 711, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 657, "last_played": 1662690542, "avatar": "190b3730fd0ba2f674e152b31bc82069e7ab2d7d"}, "language": "english", "review": "retrofuturistic L4D2 clone. it's bare bones right now, but it's pretty fun.\n\n^this was my positive review for 2 years, because i thought they'd make it into a game. i liked the idea of it, but i actually thought it'd eventually become something worthwhile.\n\nyour team gives early access a bad name.", "timestamp_created": 1658517405, "timestamp_updated": 1717619361, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.507625401020050049", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "119197209", "author": {"steamid": "76561197960909121", "personaname": "♛ taïk^", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/DavinciPGM/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 67, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 67, "last_played": 1656703302, "avatar": "190e631fb3216440fcf4740224c48361e0c220f4"}, "language": "english", "review": "A Masterclass in Unoriginality: Why This Game is Left for Dead in Space\n\nAh, the audacity of hope—or should I say, the audacity of copy-paste? Here we have a game that boldly goes where every game has gone before, a veritable shrine to the art of Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V. Picture this: Left For Dead 2, but in space. Yes, you heard that right. Someone decided that the only thing missing from the zombie apocalypse was a lack of oxygen and zero gravity.\n\nThe developers must have been in a boardroom, brainstorming, when someone had the epiphany: \"What if we take Left For Dead 2, slap on some spacesuits, replace the zombies with aliens that suspiciously act like zombies, and call it a day?\" Standing ovation. Champagne corks popped. A new game was born—or rather, an old game was reheated in the microwave of mediocrity.\n\nThe mechanics? Oh, they're as original as a plagiarized thesis. You shoot, you run, you reload. Rinse and repeat until you question the very essence of your gaming life. The aliens? They're zombies in extraterrestrial drag, clawing at you with the same mind-numbing predictability. It's as if the game is daring you to find something—anything—novel in its cosmic corridors.\n\nAnd let's talk about the price. Ah, the price! For the low, low cost of too much, you too can own this masterpiece of monotony. It's like buying a designer knockoff at a premium price, only to realize you could've had the real deal for less.\n\nIn conclusion, if you're looking for a game that challenges the very definition of the word 'new,' look no further. But if you value originality, excitement, and not feeling like you've been conned by intergalactic highway robbers, then do yourself a favor: get Left For Dead 2. It's the game this one wishes it could be when it grows up.", "timestamp_created": 1658408401, "timestamp_updated": 1693983670, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 5, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.470121026039123535", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "119110912", "author": {"steamid": "76561197977722228", "personaname": "TurboSpeedButton", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/TurboSpeedButton/", "num_games_owned": 201, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 1002, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 712, "last_played": 1673233399, "avatar": "feb4c9f039c00f96e9eaf56fefa5c75a7be04b63"}, "language": "english", "review": "Every time I've played this game I've had a lot of fun", "timestamp_created": 1658285493, "timestamp_updated": 1658285493, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.487495362758636475", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "119016080", "author": {"steamid": "76561198012276314", "personaname": "Pixel Paintbrush", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198012276314/", "num_games_owned": 739, "num_reviews": 82, "playtime_forever": 761, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 267, "last_played": 1721341197, "avatar": "eecb34e26ea59067475bc411c73da82162960079"}, "language": "english", "review": "A very fun Sci-Fi romp that is easily reminiscent of L4D.  Albeit with a ,60’s twist.   The guns could use some work, but other than that I found the 3 campaigns to be VERY enjoyable and not outstay their welcome   The enemies are ok, but I could swear they used to be lizard men….if not then someone should make a lizardman.  \n\nIs it perfect? No\nDoes it have heart? Yup!\nWith more time and polish this could be an instant classic for sci-fi B movie lovers, oh also it runs on Steam Deck!", "timestamp_created": 1658158610, "timestamp_updated": 1658158610, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.487495362758636475", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": true, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "118886113", "author": {"steamid": "76561198017612459", "personaname": "cobaye", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/latiasgirl/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 3, "playtime_forever": 129, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 129, "last_played": 1647154243, "avatar": "afe78a2ca1cd61c8da2ce27c1343bd2644952631"}, "language": "english", "review": "game is really fun!!! I like it when the gun shooty", "timestamp_created": 1657945682, "timestamp_updated": 1657945682, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.472689062356948853", "comment_c